 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Traditionally holy basil; most restaurants outside Thailand use Thai basil, which tastes like regular basil with a hint of aniseed.</li><li>Regular basil works too.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Basil"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Two bird’s eye chillies give a good buzz without blowing your head off.</li><li>Adjust to taste, or add a dollop of chilli paste with the chicken instead.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Chilli"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Light and dark soy can both be swapped for all-purpose soy, or the dark for more light.</li><li>Never use all dark soy — far too strong.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Soy sauce"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>For hot buckwheat noodles, see <a href=\"curry-soba.html\">curry soba</a> or <a href=\"kake-soba.html\">hot soba noodle soup</a>.</p>",
   "title_html": "Soba instead?"
  }
 ],
